uston)","fallback":"\u2014","note":"Now grab a defense with a good Week-1 matchup."},{"rd":15,"pick":171,"window":"Streamers","target":"Kicker (any high-scoring offense)","fallback":"\u2014","note":"Kicker last. Stream both DST & K weekly."}],"scenarios":["DEFAULT (you took a WR at 3): leave the 22/27 turn with an RB anchor + one more stud.  Ideal pairs: Walker + Nabers  \u00b7  Hampton + Kyren  \u00b7  Jacobs + Olave.","CHASE AND NACUA BOTH GONE AT 3: take Jaxon Smith-Njigba. Do NOT reach for an RB at 3 \u2014 the Tier-1 WR still wins the pick.","GIBBS OR BIJAN SLIDES TO 3: take him. Then go WR + WR at 22/27 (A.J. Brown / Nico + Nabers / Flowers) \u2014 your RB1 is already banked.","JEANTY FALLS TO 22: that's an ankle discount, not a red flag \u2014 take him if you can stomach 'questionable' Week 1; otherwise Walker is the safe anchor."],"faab":[{"rule":"Save it for RBs","detail":"Most FAAB league-winners are backup RBs who fall into a starting job (injury or benching). Spend your biggest bids there, not on WRs."},{"rule":"Be aggressive early (Wks 1-4)","detail":"This is when breakout RB/WRs first surface and roles shift. Pounce on real opportunity \u2014 but don't empty the tank."},{"rule":"Cap any single bid","detail":"Rarely go over ~$30-40 on one player unless it's a clear league-winner (a true every-down bell-cow RB)."},{"rule":"Keep dry powder","detail":"Hold ~$25-30 into the fantasy playoff push (Wks 12-14) for an injury replacement or a great matchup streamer."},{"rule":"Win ties with odd bids","detail":"Bid $17 or $23, never round numbers \u2014 you edge out everyone parked on $15 / $20."},{"rule":"Stream K & DST cheap","detail":"Kickers, defenses, and one-week fill-ins are $0-2 bids. Never pay up for those."},{"rule":"Don't panic Week 1","detail":"Let roles settle a week or two before spending on preseason hype or one big game."}]}